// The bodies call these UNQUALIFIED. The decompiler printed them as members of
// the concrete instantiation -- `std::_Rb_tree<...>::find(...)`,
// `std::_Rb_tree<...>::_M_erase(...)` -- and the transcription dropped the
// class part entirely, leaving a bare `find(...)`. SexyAppBase.cpp alone had
// fifteen C3861s from `find` / `_M_erase` / `_M_erase_aux` / `_M_insert_unique`
// / `_M_insert_unique_`, and Board and ResourceManager hit the same thing.
//
// Naming them here fixes every such call site at once. There is no ambiguity:
// no translation unit in this project does `using namespace std;`, so a bare
// `find(...)` can only mean this one.
