// PakLib::Driver -- the archive driver, a DIFFERENT class from Sexy::Driver.
//
// The two live in different places in the binary and the demangled names say
// so: Sexy::Driver's members sit at 0x409D4C..0x409E08, while this one's are
// at 0x444268..0x4442A0 next to PakLib::DriverFactory. The transcription
// merged them into Sexy/Driver.h, which is why the bodies there could not name
// their own class.
//
// The constructor at 0x444268 fixes the layout:
//
//     object vtable is installed by the constructor
//     the name, a 4-byte string, is copied at +4
//     the priority is stored at +8
//
// so the object is three words. GetPriority reads +8; GetName copies the name
// at +4 into the caller's destination.
//
// Phase 1 converted the opaque storage into named members. The transcription wrote
// a 0x20 byte array and noted "Was 0xC" itself: the largest offset any body of this
// class reaches is +8, so the object is 0x0C and the extra 0x14 bytes were the
// transcriber's own padding. The vtable pointer is written by the constructor
// so the class is polymorphic and the vptr is left to the compiler;
// there is no out-of-line destructor for it in this tree, hence `= default`.
class Driver
{
public:
    virtual ~Driver() = default;

    Sexy::String mName;     // +0x04  copied in by the constructor
    int          mPriority; // +0x08  GetPriority returns it
    // Size 0x0C.

    Driver(Sexy::String theName, int thePriority);
    // The parameter is the destination the name is copied into.
    Driver* GetName(int theDest);
    int GetPriority();
};

